  "structure": {
    "block_count": 77,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "How to Create a Night Shift System When You Have a Newborn",
        "text_sha256": "02f675aa174bb4f3c2ee17ccfae18608aff34740f09db5340d5a192af6840685",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "creating a night shift system with a newborn",
        "text_sha256": "31237373ace93bf55fbfa61da79b751c831c1de0dba8685f7d2c678be183b2dc",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "One way parents of newborn babies can get a little more sleep is by taking shifts at night.",
        "text_sha256": "ead75787fd87393b56d2c68b2916f2caec0f1d106b6f4b2e05989accdcd16c30",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Sleep is never easy to come by in those hazy newborn days. But one way parents can get a little more of it is by taking shifts at night.",
        "text_sha256": "64d8e311741ef809fc5781a31fb4a2aabf4bf407c42de6be915853d5a0f4b465",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Read on for different ways families can manage nighttime feedings with a newborn, including sample schedules.",
        "text_sha256": "003662b998517668ffd97af63bb6480c4debad52a67d89d6a134c24f7855d883",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What is a newborn night shift system?",
        "text_sha256": "9d752736f0efb4b3b7419f18a195f3dd0e8dc8d9215c0e353b3244ce77f2ffea",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "During the newborn days, many couples opt to establish a night shift system where each parent takes turns caring for the baby. Parents alternate baby care duties, such as overnight feeds, diaper changes, burping and getting baby back to bed.",
        "text_sha256": "02e760af1fae0d88daf2cc92eb5884ad5a29a6088158ba470316e64ed39e4c37",
        "word_count": 40
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Night shift systems don't necessarily work for every family, including single parents and families where one parent works overnight. But in two-parent households where both partners have a similar schedule, splitting up those late-night duties can help everyone feel more rested, as well as give non-birthing parents more opportunities to bond with baby. The extra sleep that comes with taking shifts can also help parents who are at risk for or are experiencing postpartum depression. Trusted SourceAmerican Academy of PediatricsDepression During & After Pregnancy: You Are Not AloneSee All Sources [1]",
        "text_sha256": "b2fcdeceeab269141a8d075fca969e9cc771d2af40ce1ad061b6113006968a8f",
        "word_count": 91
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceAmerican Academy of PediatricsDepression During & After Pregnancy: You Are Not AloneSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "95021c93694a8556dd8f7af8ef8d38f7d000d119fba1dadd5283591f3d601276",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "But parents aren't the only ones who can take on nighttime duties. You might ask other family members or friends to be on call overnight — a move that can be especially helpful for single parents or families where one parent works at night. Hiring a night nurse can be another option, if it's financially feasible.",
        "text_sha256": "4de750cb979f0d986e3e71bd0c160c2616c25939ca82cbc6c73f419a4b55a731",
        "word_count": 56
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Figuring out the right night shift system for your family depends on how you're feeding your baby, and it can take some trial and error. Here are some sample schedules to help you get started, plus tips for making the plan work for everyone.",
        "text_sha256": "6e8ec33c7850f65463f08a06235780407e67e8c1d19a8b00cf754b86de0ff6ec",
        "word_count": 44
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Sample baby night shift schedules",
        "text_sha256": "f2e9ea808d1cc9f1849144088984544136b20b536a0d765fa560e0fa72e45680",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Just as there's no \"right\" way to feed your baby, there's no one-size-fits-all nighttime schedule when you have a newborn. Some families breastfeed exclusively ; others supplement with formula or exclusively pump and bottle-feed; others formula-feed from day one. All these feeding methods deliver the nourishment a baby needs to grow and thrive.",
        "text_sha256": "2dce2b629c1a3b6574f848f1ea455b8d77d1e990d9740bac0a3bfa46f06d949e",
        "word_count": 53
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Shift times will vary depending on how your baby is fed. (Exclusively breastfeeding moms, for instance, will be up more often than parents who exclusively use formula.) You and your partner's individual needs and preferences will factor in, too.",
        "text_sha256": "677a85e9532b542931c51396f6115d0fd8d94da23bbde2bbfe598f85e6504b4f",
        "word_count": 39
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "These schedules will also vary depending on your baby's age and how often she's sleeping and eating at night, as well as other variables (how long it takes her to fall back asleep, for example). Still, the sample schedules below can help provide a jumping-off point to figure out a system that works for your family.",
        "text_sha256": "cdff39cd3adf7b73f3b837bb459d93e8e089d44dacbcda98823daf206f840382",
        "word_count": 56
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Sample night shift schedule for a formula-feeding family",
        "text_sha256": "2101642037b7e1dbd908eea09df1ef415c3c4e752660e317b735ca9169f14b87",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Formula-feeding offers the most flexibility for families wanting to take nighttime shifts. Since parents can share feeding responsibilities equally, each person gets the ability to snooze for longer stretches. Trusted SourceAmerican Academy of PediatricsAmount and Schedule of Formula FeedingsSee All Sources [2]",
        "text_sha256": "6355d7bbcf8c3dd9f5f27c4a8c16dafbe9ebd0c01eb29079970e374e94fa4f82",
        "word_count": 42
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceAmerican Academy of PediatricsAmount and Schedule of Formula FeedingsSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "1383cefaa6f3e4c155b23fe80d3754087f84a7848747c5e8531591a651d3a80c",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "7:00 P.M.: Parent 1 gives baby a formula bottle",
        "text_sha256": "b99511d4a1b5944c2bee90d3903f08d03112f1d8c51f3fb68141de89c1d284b7",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "8:00 P.M.: Both parents go to bed",
        "text_sha256": "61fbceef04f0ae54726bc46a458e4e7faee84ff545c1493704a4621864ac5491",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "10:00 P.M.: Parent 2 gives baby a formula bottle",
        "text_sha256": "9041a7d52d9c26c95ce0f376b7174439327fb8072cad6a4c95a91e6c1782ceeb",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "11:00 P.M.: Parent 2 goes to bed",
        "text_sha256": "2eea1dbfd91fb1be6d25fdc82b829869e2779ce70c7a49f907dc3e61e408a6f7",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "1:00 A.M.: Parent 1 gives baby a formula bottle",
        "text_sha256": "9e953cc7c388a722db20644d8d9b739a1c988aa0039b2d87a7e47e0b00261aef",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "2:00 A.M.: Parent 1 goes to bed",
        "text_sha256": "72cf558b5b50b2364ca5be5fda0ca72fa2011e2c6a9de0bb8035be4165ad5d01",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "4:00 A.M.: Parent 2 gives baby a formula bottle",
        "text_sha256": "dbf075c927358cfc46bcf2a1b1bbcfb51fc50cfe4351fb609183b215dcb5b8d2",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "5:00 A.M.: Parent 2 goes to bed",
        "text_sha256": "6de751836a61a43e5d57662f5c52c0618ef66d71300657eba0173e85e3c38143",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "7:00 A.M.: Parent 1 gives baby a formula bottle",
        "text_sha256": "0419a60bc7a7b0762a83f078f7877fbfcd75dc9d35cb29122518934428a23051",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "(Note: This schedule assumes baby is a formula-fed newborn eating roughly every three to four hours. It also assumes that it takes about an hour to complete each feeding session, though in reality it may take a little more or less time for everyone to get back to sleep.)",
        "text_sha256": "9edda150365becbcc240e56dc46706b095bb72bfcce7ed28350df59cc57d7836",
        "word_count": 49
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Sample night shift schedule for a combo-feeding family",
        "text_sha256": "2577b19e307369e4cd5deb0c6721f5d708548146644b782c34888494c658183a",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Switching between breast milk and formula bottles, also known as combo feeding, gives breastfeeding mothers some overnight flexibility, since they're not on duty for every feeding. Trusted SourceKidsHealth From NemoursBreastfeeding FAQs: Solids and SupplementingSee All Sources [3]",
        "text_sha256": "2dcf297844bb7df54afdd528e9cf037ee56aa3f7012e2ffe74e38dae488c46db",
        "word_count": 37
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceKidsHealth From NemoursBreastfeeding FAQs: Solids and SupplementingSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "56077e779b8994cbad089b2b5310a26b93849c5b239eba70a4c6bd95b1836a8f",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "However, sleeping longer stretches could up the odds for feeling engorged , especially if your baby is a newborn and you're still establishing your milk supply . You might opt to wake during each feeding and pump (some mothers find that this is a little faster than nursing, and it lets you go back to sleep immediately after pumping while the other parent handles baby care and cleans the pump parts).",
        "text_sha256": "cbd7b82a3ff5bb0611d878c98d0b135895b9068eaefe96e1aa59dfdf17ee4caf",
        "word_count": 71
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "7:00 P.M.: Mom breastfeeds baby",
        "text_sha256": "b2d342aa92ba6f9b34719a8807be281c7ffebf9eef22f22645df9e5a9a1b86aa",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "8:00 P.M.: Mom goes to bed",
        "text_sha256": "4745384d31f4666af8dae4419177e044f2f9d35adc10d83cd94915777b77d3cb",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000034",
        "block_index": 34,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "10:00 P.M.: Non-birthing parent gives baby a formula bottle",
        "text_sha256": "121122c26c1c8769e5a59aa49767827669aa7a1a0f286a149b49a44d58fe6dd7",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000035",
