        "text_sha256": "08298b8b56bfccf7549dc51754d7c09c7a427b647638052658c67434dbdd3531",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000052",
        "block_index": 52,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "7:00 A.M.: Mom pumps, then gives bottle to baby",
        "text_sha256": "8530d8705d206947c115e81327524727b804284537d9df8144af6928ee29ef68",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000053",
        "block_index": 53,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "(Note: This schedule assumes the baby is a newborn who is bottle-fed breast milk roughly every two to three hours. However, your little one may want to eat more often than this during the night. It also assumes that it takes about an hour to complete each feeding session, though in reality it may take a little more or less time for everyone to get back to sleep.)",
        "text_sha256": "6407970aadd9108df25b9046d4e84549039f5e241d0d02c4e0878f3ebbd35bdc",
        "word_count": 68
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000054",
        "block_index": 54,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Sample night shift schedule for a breastfeeding family",
        "text_sha256": "100a9a878821b0815400c4fe0e8de70b7ac648d805f25d5ce4f4c2291f47affa",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000055",
        "block_index": 55,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Moms who are exclusively breastfeeding will need to be up for every feeding during the night. But they can still maximize their sleep time if the non-birthing parent takes on the non-feeding duties like changing, burping and getting baby back to sleep. Trusted SourceAmerican College of Obstetricians and GynecologistsBreastfeeding Your BabySee All Sources [4]",
        "text_sha256": "a49083bedfbddfe49dec0fcfa650e1b98f91b3412030a215dcc9f090216c8bfa",
        "word_count": 54
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000056",
        "block_index": 56,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceAmerican College of Obstetricians and GynecologistsBreastfeeding Your BabySee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "ce7e258b13497a79259148261796afeccccfa4f595777a8f72b3e0a4e83e215b",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000057",
        "block_index": 57,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "7:00 P.M.: Mom breastfeeds baby",
        "text_sha256": "b2d342aa92ba6f9b34719a8807be281c7ffebf9eef22f22645df9e5a9a1b86aa",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000058",
